        "probe": "Map slots, clearance, exposed edge and pickup access; verify bolt fit, strip bendability and sub-millimetre pocket play before fabrication. Abandon infeasible geometry. Drill strips only; do not drill, cut, heat or glue plate/carriage; expose the marked 30 mm edge, avoid stroke clearance and keep carriage on rails. Within 80 fabrication/20 observation minutes, build at most pocket and clamp; perform up to three twenty-stroke runs and three gloved removal/return checks each. Record displacement and qualitative seating pressure; use spare for final run. Require <=60 seconds and no marked-edge contact. Stop on intrusion or necessary edge contact.",
        "uncertainty": "Slot geometry, strip stiffness, supplied hardware and unmarked pickup access remain unverified. Stroke duration may force fewer runs, reducing confidence. Pull-scale escape comparisons up to 10 N cannot establish resistance to unknown stroke forces. The 3 N versus 7 N magnetic anomaly motivates reduced magnetic dependence; it proves neither retention nor serviceability."
